    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d455-a2">

                <pb facs="0550" n="462" sameAs="frus:frus1904/pg462"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 2.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Clayton to Mr. Mariscal.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >American Embassy</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Mexico</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1904-01-14"
                                ><hi rendition="#italic">January 14,
                    1904</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Mr. Minister</hi>: I have the honor to transmit,
                    herewith, a copy of a telegram of yesterday from the American consul at
                    Matamoros concerning the arrest of the American citizens H. C. Harding and H. E.
                    Dugat at that place.</p>
                <p>According to the consul’s statement, which I have every reason to believe to be
                    correct, the offense would seem to be of a trival character, not meriting such
                    harsh treatment.</p>
                <p>I beg that your excellency will take such prompt action, by telegraph, as will
                    lead to a proper disposition of this case.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Powell Clayton.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
